  <CodeBlock code={statusEnum} title="NotificationPermissionStatus.swift" />

  <h2>NotificationPermissionObserving Protocol</h2>
  <p>The protocol provides the current status and a stream. Since iOS provides no system callback when the user changes notification permission in Settings, the observer re-checks the status on every app foreground event.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={observingProtocol} title="NotificationPermissionObserving.swift" />

  <h2>Helper Extensions</h2>
  <p>The protocol includes convenience computed properties for the most common permission states.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={helperExtensions} title="NotificationPermissionObserving+Helpers.swift" />

